    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Brendan Kearns, Hills Property, is pleased to present this prominent mixed-use property on Main Street (N56), Stranorlar, Co. Donegal to the market.\r\n\r\nThe standout feature of this property is the substantial 100m² first-floor accommodation, which is currently vacant and offers excellent potential for residential redevelopment in the heart of Stranorlar.\r\n\r\nWith a strong demand for housing throughout the area, purchasers may be able to avail of significant government funding, including the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant (up to €50,000), the Vacant Above the Shop Grant (up to €115,000, subject to eligibility and approval) and a range of SEAI home energy upgrade grants, presenting an opportunity to create much-needed town centre living accommodation while substantially reducing refurbishment costs.\r\n\r\nThe ground floor extends to approximately 90m² and is currently occupied as a retail unit, providing an existing commercial element while the upper floor offers scope for residential conversion, refurbishment, or reconfiguration.\r\n\r\nLocated on one of the busiest thoroughfares in County Donegal, the property also benefits from exceptional visibility, with weekday traffic volumes estimated at between 8,692 vehicles (south of Stranorlar) and 11,416 vehicles (north of Stranorlar) per day.\r\n\r\nProperties offering this combination of town centre location, vacant upper-floor accommodation, grant funding potential, and existing commercial space are seldom brought to the market."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
